<section class="wrap section section--flush" id="problem" aria-labelledby="problem-title">
  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
      <h2 id="problem-title">FOI statistics are published, but turning them into a reliable view takes work</h2>
      <ul class="quotes quotes--solo"><li><figure><blockquote><p>Missing data is shown, not invented.</p></blockquote><figcaption class="cite"><strong>Bluebird FOI Insights</strong>How to use</figcaption></figure></li></ul>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="copy">
        <p>Every year, Australian Government agencies and ministers report their FOI activity: requests received, decisions made, and how quickly they were made. Demand rose sharply in 2024-25: 42,759 requests were received, up 25.2% and the highest of the six complete years published.</p>
        <p>The statistics arrive as a series of workbooks, one per year, with layouts that vary between releases. Agencies are renamed, courts merge and a year's file can be reissued. Turning that into a reliable view of performance and compliance takes time, and a figure that can't be traced to its source is hard to defend.</p>
      </div>
      <figure class="chart">
        <figcaption>
          <h3 class="chart-title">FOI requests received, by financial year</h3>
          <p class="chart-sub">Requests received from applicants. 2025-26 covers July to March only, so it is hatched and is not comparable with complete years.</p>
        </figcaption>
