<section class="band-navy" id="how" aria-labelledby="how-title">
  <div class="wrap section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
      <h2 id="how-title">Every figure is computed from the source data</h2>
      <p>The platform computes each number from the Australian Government's published FOI statistics. The only exceptions are eight headline figures transcribed from the OAIC dashboard.</p>
    </div>
    <ol class="flow" style="--n:5">
      <li><h3>Pin the sources</h3><p>Seven agency workbooks, 2019-20 to 2025-26, are pinned with their publication date and SHA-256 hash.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Normalise</h3><p>Each sheet is read into facts by agency, measure and request type. Every batch is stamped with the normaliser version and a content hash.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Check at start-up</h3><p>The platform re-sums its facts against the published totals every time it starts. A mismatch stops the service rather than showing a wrong page.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Compute</h3><p>Figures are computed from the facts. The eight Q1 2025-26 headline figures transcribed from the OAIC dashboard are also checked at start-up.</p></li>
      <li><h3>Serve with provenance</h3><p>Each figure appears with its basis label and a link to where it came from. The same figures are available through a read-only API.</p></li>
    </ol>
    <div class="boundary">
      <div>
        <h3>Chat and reports</h3>
        <p>A signed-in Chat and reports section is available by invitation.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="never">
        <h3>What the platform is built to do</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Keep models out of the figures:</strong> the API returns "nothing a model generated", only the canonical data and the figures computed from it.</li>
          <li><strong>Show gaps as gaps:</strong> a measure the source doesn't publish shows "No published data for this measure".</li>
          <li><strong>Stop on a mismatch:</strong> a failed start-up check stops the service.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="boundary-note">As stated in the demo's reference pages.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="band-mist" id="inside" aria-labelledby="inside-title">
  <div class="wrap section" data-acc-scope>
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside the product</p>
      <h2 id="inside-title">Every view, and what it shows</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="acc-head">
      <h3>Views</h3>
      <button type="button" class="btn-text" data-expand-all hidden><span class="js-label">Expand all</span><span class="visually-hidden"> views</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="points">
      <details id="foi-overview"><summary><span class="acc-title">FOI at a glance</span><span class="hint">The headline view</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <p>Headline figures for the latest complete year, year-on-year tables, a "What the data says" summary computed from the same figures as the charts, and a separate panel for the latest single quarter.</p>
        <p>A compliance ranking lists agencies by the share of decisions made within the statutory period. Agencies that decided fewer than 30 requests are shown with their rates but not ranked.</p>
      </div></details>
      <details id="foi-requests"><summary><span class="acc-title">Requests</span><span class="hint">Received, contributions and finalised</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Requests received from applicants, with requests received on transfer from another agency shown as their own measure.</li>
          <li>Key agency contributions to requests received.</li>
          <li>Requests finalised.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></details>
      <details id="foi-decisions"><summary><span class="acc-title">Decisions</span><span class="hint">What was decided, and how outcomes moved</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Requests decided, and key agency contributions.</li>
          <li>Decision outcomes: granted in full, granted in part, refused and withdrawn.</li>
          <li>Change in decision outcomes year on year.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></details>
      <details id="foi-timeliness"><summary><span class="acc-title">Timeliness</span><span class="hint">Decisions within the statutory period</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li>Timeliness: the share of decisions made within the statutory period.</li>
          <li>Change in timeliness year on year.</li>
          <li>Compliance by agency.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></details>
      <details id="foi-reference"><summary><span class="acc-title">Reference</span><span class="hint">Notes, guidance, API and provenance</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Data notes:</strong> the publisher's own notes and disclaimer, reproduced verbatim, plus the platform's reconciliation notes.</li>
          <li><strong>How to use:</strong> how to read the basis labels, filters and gaps.</li>
          <li><strong>API access:</strong> the endpoints behind every chart.</li>
          <li><strong>Data provenance:</strong> every source file, hash, derivation and curation decision.</li>
        </ul>
      </div></details>
      <details id="foi-chat-reports"><summary><span class="acc-title">Chat and reports</span><span class="hint">Signed-in, by invitation</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <p>A signed-in section of the demo. Access is by invitation through Bluebird.</p>
      </div></details>
      <details id="foi-api"><summary><span class="acc-title">API</span><span class="hint">The same figures, as read-only JSON</span></summary><div class="acc-body">
        <p>Every figure and fact behind the charts is available as a read-only JSON API:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><code>/api/</code>: dataset information, measures and source link.</li>
          <li><code>/api/figures</code>: every computed figure with its basis label.</li>
          <li><code>/api/facts</code>: the underlying facts, filterable by financial year, measure, request type, agency and quarter.</li>
          <li><code>/api/measures</code>: the measure groups.</li>
          <li><code>/api/provenance</code>: the provenance registry, including any one figure's basis.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The public demo API is rate-limited and tuned for demo traffic.</p>
      </div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

