      <p class="eyebrow">Trust and security</p>
      <h2 id="trust-title">Every figure can be traced and checked</h2>
    </div>
    <dl class="facts facts--icons">
      <div><dt class="ic ic--database">Data used</dt><dd>Published, aggregate statistics only, from the data.gov.au Freedom of information statistics dataset.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--link">Traceability</dt><dd>Every figure links to its provenance: the source file, its hash, the derivation and the curation decisions behind it.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--check">Integrity checks</dt><dd>Start-up checks re-sum the facts against published totals. A mismatch stops the service.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--minus">Gaps</dt><dd>Measures the source doesn't publish are shown as missing, never as zero.</dd></div>
      <div><dt class="ic ic--sliders">Fair comparison</dt><dd>Agencies that decided fewer than 30 requests are shown with their rates, not ranked.</dd></div>
      </dl>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="wrap section" id="questions" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
  <div data-acc-scope>
    <div class="acc-head">
      <h2 id="questions-title">Common questions</h2>
      <button type="button" class="btn-text" data-expand-all hidden><span class="js-label">Expand all</span><span class="visually-hidden"> questions</span></button>
    </div>
    <div class="points">
      <details id="q-foi-source"><summary><span class="acc-title">Where does the data come from?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>From the agency FOI workbooks in the Freedom of information statistics dataset on data.gov.au, maintained by the OAIC. Eight single-quarter headline figures for Q1 2025-26 come from the OAIC's published dashboard, because they can't be derived from the cumulative workbook.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-foi-current"><summary><span class="acc-title">How current is it?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>The latest complete financial year is 2024-25. 2025-26 is published so far as July to March, and is never compared with full years. The sources were last verified on 13 September 2026.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-foi-ai"><summary><span class="acc-title">Does AI produce any of the figures?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>No. Every figure is computed from the published data. The API returns nothing a model generated.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-foi-ranking"><summary><span class="acc-title">Why are some agencies not ranked?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>A rate based on a handful of decisions can swing widely. Agencies that decided fewer than 30 requests in either year being compared are shown with their rates but left out of the ranking.</p></div></details>
      <details id="q-foi-api"><summary><span class="acc-title">Can we use the figures in our own tools?</span></summary><div class="acc-body"><p>Yes. A read-only JSON API exposes the same figures and facts the pages show. The public demo API is rate-limited for demo traffic.</p></div></details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

